=== (6) nested chi-cut attempt: generator symbol g = k*c(k) (edge decoupled smoothly); identity g(k+q)-g(k) = theta(q) on {F^{0j}(k,k+q) != 0} ===
c=1 on |k|<=2.0, 0 beyond 2.6: q=0.009971: max_k |g(k+q)-g(k)-q| on support = 8.262e-02 (= 8.29 q); best constant theta: spread of g(k+q)-g(k) on support = 8.262e-02
c=1 on |k|<=2.0, 0 beyond 2.6: q=0.0009587: max_k |g(k+q)-g(k)-q| on support = 7.945e-03 (= 8.29 q); best constant theta: spread of g(k+q)-g(k) on support = 7.945e-03
c=1 on |k|<=2.5, 0 beyond 3.0: q=0.009971: max_k |g(k+q)-g(k)-q| on support = 1.155e-01 (= 11.59 q); best constant theta: spread of g(k+q)-g(k) on support = 1.155e-01
c=1 on |k|<=2.5, 0 beyond 3.0: q=0.0009587: max_k |g(k+q)-g(k)-q| on support = 1.111e-02 (= 11.59 q); best constant theta: spread of g(k+q)-g(k) on support = 1.111e-02
c=1 on |k|<=2.9, 0 beyond 3.1: q=0.009971: max_k |g(k+q)-g(k)-q| on support = 3.042e-01 (= 30.51 q); best constant theta: spread of g(k+q)-g(k) on support = 3.042e-01
c=1 on |k|<=2.9, 0 beyond 3.1: q=0.0009587: max_k |g(k+q)-g(k)-q| on support = 2.927e-02 (= 30.53 q); best constant theta: spread of g(k+q)-g(k) on support = 2.927e-02
A continuous g that equals k on the box must return to 0 somewhere on the coupled set: the identity fails there at O(q).

